    "body": "The config loader retry tests patched attributes of Python's shared `time` module. Calls from unrelated consumers could enter the retry mock: the unit shard observed 509 sleep calls instead of two.\n\nIsolate the loader's `time` reference with a wrapping mock before applying the existing sleep and jitter patches. Add a parametrized regression that injects unrelated sleeps and retains the exact retry-count and backoff assertions. Runtime code is unchanged.\n\nValidation:\n- Deterministic fail-before: the injected case fails with five sleep calls instead of two; 24 other cases pass.\n- Pass-after, including after the main refresh: all 25 focused tests pass.\n- Local source-loading harness bypassed eager package initializers because the available container's MCore is older; the actual loader and compatibility module were loaded from this checkout. This does not establish full CI success.\n- All-file pre-commit, `git diff --check`, and independent review passed.\n\nCause: **3. Bridge bug** — test mocks modified shared standard-library state. No upstream Megatron-LM PR is causal. The exact background caller behind CI's 509 calls is not established; the isolation defect is reproduced independently.\n\nHuman review and successful current-head CI are required before merge.\n",
    "changed_files": 1,
